From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mxc: gpu-viv: Declare _QuerySignal with its real return type

gc_hal_kernel_linux.h prototypes _QuerySignal() as returning gctBOOL, but
the function is defined in gc_hal_kernel_os.c as returning gceSTATUS. The
two disagree: gctBOOL is an integer typedef, gceSTATUS an enum. GCC 14
turned that into a hard error (-Werror=enum-int-mismatch, on by default
since it was promoted from a warning), so the driver no longer builds:

  gc_hal_kernel_os.c:5703:1: error: conflicting types for '_QuerySignal'
  due to enum/integer mismatch; have 'gceSTATUS(struct _gckOS *, void *)'

The definition is the correct one, and both call sites already agree with
it: gc_hal_kernel_sync.c stores the result in a gceSTATUS and tests it
with gcmIS_ERROR() and against gcvSTATUS_TRUE, neither of which is a
gctBOOL operation. Only the prototype is wrong, so correct it there.

No functional change: the two types have the same size and the generated
code is unchanged; this only makes the declaration match the definition.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no upstream]

The nxp-qoriq/linux 5.4 branch this BSP pins (LSDK 20.04) is no longer
maintained, and drivers/mxc/gpu-viv is a vendor driver that was never in
mainline, so there is no upstream to send this to.

Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 drivers/mxc/gpu-viv/hal/os/linux/kernel/gc_hal_kernel_linux.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mxc/gpu-viv/hal/os/linux/kernel/gc_hal_kernel_linux.h b/drivers/mxc/gpu-viv/hal/os/linux/kernel/gc_hal_kernel_linux.h
--- a/drivers/mxc/gpu-viv/hal/os/linux/kernel/gc_hal_kernel_linux.h
+++ b/drivers/mxc/gpu-viv/hal/os/linux/kernel/gc_hal_kernel_linux.h
@@ -311,7 +311,7 @@ _ConvertLogical2Physical(
     OUT gctPHYS_ADDR_T * Physical
     );
 
-gctBOOL
+gceSTATUS
 _QuerySignal(
     IN gckOS Os,
     IN gctSIGNAL Signal
